  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x1000" flags="0x0">
    <title>Rev limit, manual (above 55 km/h) (id_n_max_mt)</title>
    <description>id_n_max_mt | free to change | risk medium&#013;&#010;Stock: 6520 to 6520 rpm&#013;&#010;Allowed by ms45_check.py: 3500 to 7000&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Engine speed where the limiter starts to act. One cell per detected gear: column 0 = no gear detected (standing, neutral), 1-6 = gears, 7 and 8 are unused.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Recipe: Higher limit: all 9 cells 6700. Same values in id_n_max_h_mt. Never above 7000.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Only active above 55 km/h plus 2 s. Below that, id_n_max_h_mt applies. Emulator: the limit follows the table value in each gear.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Together with: Always set to the same values as id_n_max_h_mt. Above 7000 rpm it collides with the over-rev counter c_n_lim_min (7200).&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Test: Warm engine, standing, briefly hit the limiter. Read fault memory afterwards.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="1" />
    <XDFAXIS id="x" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x5251" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="8" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <units></units>
      <indexcount>9</indexcount>
      <decimalpl>0</decimalpl>
      <embedinfo type="1" />
      <datatype>0</datatype>
      <unittype>0</unittype>
      <DALINK index="0" />
      <MATH equation="X">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
    </XDFAXIS>
    <XDFAXIS id="y" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="-32" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <units>-</units>
      <indexcount>1</indexcount>
      <decimalpl>0</decimalpl>
      <outputtype>2</outputtype>
      <datatype>0</datatype>
      <unittype>0</unittype>
      <DALINK index="0" />
      <LABEL index="0" value="" />
